    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2002-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring \\(3x-2\\) from the first two terms, \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(3x - 2)\\big[(4x + 1) - 4x\\big] + 1 \\\\ &= (3x - 2)(1) + 1 \\\\ &= 3x - 1. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nAt \\(x = 4,\\) this equals \\(3\\cdot4 - 1 = 11.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(3x - 2\\) out of the first two terms before plugging in",
        "The bracket \\((4x + 1) - 4x\\) collapses to \\(1\\)"
      ],
